/// imported
state investigation: "Pre-Charge Investigation" by applicant cite Fed. R. Crim. P. 41; 18 U.S.C. § 3282
  effective [2024-12-01, ..)
{
  group investigation-group
  note "Search warrants (Rule 41) require probable cause before a magistrate judge. The five-year statute of limitations in 18 U.S.C. § 3282 applies to non-capital federal offenses, measured from the offense date, not from discovery of the crime — a trap when investigating old conduct."
  _ "Present case to grand jury" -> grand-jury-convened {
    authority cite Fed. R. Crim. P. 6(a)
    effort 40.hours
    note "Hours: BigLaw-honest estimate for the effort of this move; basis: estimate."
  }
  _ "File criminal complaint" -> complaint-filed {
    authority cite ?("Fed. R. Crim. P. 3, 4")
    effort 5.hours
    cost 0.usd
    note "Hours: BigLaw-honest estimate for the effort of this move; basis: estimate. No filing fee: the district court civil filing fee (28 U.S.C. § 1914(a); District Court Miscellaneous Fee Schedule) applies only to civil actions, and Fed. R. Crim. P. 3/4 impose no fee for a criminal complaint."
  }
}

/// imported
state grand-jury-convened: "Grand Jury Convened" by office cite ?("Fed. R. Crim. P. 6(a), (e)") effective [2024-12-01, ..) {
  group investigation-group
  note "Grand jury proceedings are sealed under Rule 6(e); the target has no right to have counsel present in the jury room. Probable cause is the standard, not proof beyond a reasonable doubt, so hearsay and comparatively weak evidence suffice."
  _ "Grand jury votes" -> grand-jury-vote { authority cite Fed. R. Crim. P. 6(f) }
}

/// imported
decision grand-jury-vote: "Grand Jury Votes" by office cite Fed. R. Crim. P. 6(f)
  effective [2024-12-01, ..)
{
  group investigation-group
  note "At least 12 of the 16-23 jurors must concur to return a true bill. If fewer than 12 concur, the foreperson must report the lack of concurrence to the magistrate judge in writing — the indictment is not effective."
  _ "Return true bill" -> indictment-returned p 0.97 { authority cite Fed. R. Crim. P. 6(f) }
  _ "Return no bill" -> no-bill p 0.03 { authority cite Fed. R. Crim. P. 6(f) }
}

/// imported
state indictment-returned: "Indictment Returned (True Bill)" by office delegable_to [CaseOrder] cite ?("Fed. R. Crim. P. 6(f), 7; U.S. Const. amend. V") effective [2024-12-01, ..) {
  group investigation-group
  note "The Fifth Amendment requires grand jury indictment for federal felonies unless waived. The indictment must be returned in open court by the foreperson and starts the Speedy Trial Act clock together with arraignment (18 U.S.C. § 3161(c)(1))."
  _ "Execute arrest warrant on indictment" -> arrest { authority cite Fed. R. Crim. P. 9 }
  _ "Schedule arraignment on indictment" -> arraignment {
    authority cite Fed. R. Crim. P. 10; 18 U.S.C. § 3161(c)(1)
    deadline 70.days {
      extendable true
      extension_authority "18 U.S.C. § 3161(h)"
      note "Trial must commence within 70 days of indictment or initial appearance, whichever is later. Missing the deadline triggers dismissal with prejudice unless § 3161(h) exclusions (motions, continuances, ends-of-justice findings) apply."
    }
    duration { min 10.5.days, mode 35.days, max 70.days }
  }
}

/// imported
terminal no-bill: "No Bill — Grand Jury Declines to Indict" by applicant outcome [win, dismissal] cite ?("Fed. R. Crim. P. 6(f); Blockburger v. United States, 284 U.S. 299 (1932)") effective [2024-12-01, ..) {
  group investigation-group
  note "Double jeopardy does not attach at the grand jury stage, so the government may re-present the same charges to a different grand jury. Jeopardy attaches only when the trial jury is sworn (or the first witness is sworn in a bench trial). PLACEHOLDER PAYOFF: $1,000,000, override per matter, treating this playthrough's dispositive outcome as a full win even though double jeopardy has not yet attached and the government could theoretically re-present (not modeled as a loop back in this playthrough's payoff)."
  valence good
  payoff 1_000_000.usd
  _ "Re-present to new grand jury" -> grand-jury-convened {
    authority cite Fed. R. Crim. P. 6(a); 18 U.S.C. § 3282
    effort 20.hours
    note "Hours: BigLaw-honest estimate for the effort of this move; basis: estimate."
  }
}

